WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.362
Where are agencies?

2
00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:04.913
The guide assumes one of two
starting points for the HR feed.

3
00:00:04.913 --> 00:00:09.628
Either the workbook's HR pipeline,
Entra inbound provisioning from HR,

4
00:00:09.628 --> 00:00:13.612
is already live, or accounts
are still created from tickets.

5
00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:17.350
Either way, Gate 2 decides
who writes each attribute.

6
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.550
For availability, Gate 2 uses nothing new.

7
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:24.094
If API-driven inbound
provisioning is the writer,

8
00:00:24.094 --> 00:00:29.886
Microsoft Learn's feature availability
page lists it in Azure for U S Government,

9
00:00:29.886 --> 00:00:32.393
as are PIM, entitlement management,

10
00:00:32.393 --> 00:00:36.975
access reviews and Lifecycle
Workflows, read on November 1, 2026.

11
00:00:36.975 --> 00:00:41.163
In GCC, Entra ID is
the commercial service.

12
00:00:41.163 --> 00:00:44.530
The interim path: where the
HR pipeline isn't live yet,

13
00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:48.288
SailPoint can't be measured
against a source of authority.

14
00:00:48.288 --> 00:00:54.240
Decide the writers now, and run Gates 3 to
6 against the HR extract the kit reads.
